	(text "Range 0: 1 k (100 uA). Range 1: 33 R (3 mA). Range 2: 1 R (100 mA). Range 3: 0.1 R (1 A).\n100 mV full scale each. The shunt of range 0 is always in circuit.\nNo gate-to-source resistors here: they would bypass a shunt.\nMultiplexer channel 1 = range 0 ... channel 4 = range 3; ranges 2 and 3 use four-terminal parts.\nRanges 0 and 1 use the same nets for force and sense: route their sense tracks from the pads.\nD7: anti-parallel low-leakage clamp for the first microseconds of a load step.\nThe multiplexer address has no pull resistors: the controller pins are pulled low at reset\n(channel 1). R48 keeps the multiplexer enabled."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d5a7a5e8-da20-5ee6-84f2-0df02817bbba")
	)
